   "error": null,
   "path": "llm",
   "reason": null,
   "text": "The published ETR (issued Sep 28, 13:30 ET) may need revising because the county total is falling, now 168,598 customers out against a peak of 1,604,454, which may not match the published median restoration estimate of 79.4 h. Several crews are still enroute, and the network map feed is stale. Outage surge signals to check in counties flagged exceeds_mcc may be data dropouts, so treat them cautiously. Per-county ETRs and per-feeder restoration times are missing.",
   "links": [
    {
     "page": "map",
     "href": "/map"
    },
    {
     "page": "crews",
     "href": "/crews"
    },
    {
     "page": "health",
     "href": "/health"
    }
   ],
   "photos": 0,
   "suggestions": [],
   "language_detected": "en",
   "prior_answers": [
    "The evidence cannot settle this, because it holds no current median restoration estimate to compare against the published estimate. The published global ETR was issued at Sep 28, 13:30 ET, with a median restoration estimate of 79.4 h. DOM 14.206 requires a revision when the median moves by more than the margin it sets, and smaller moves are logged but not released. [1] As ETR Specialist you propose any revision on F-DOM-121, and the Incident Commander and the Duty Manager sign it. [2] County customers out are 168,598 and falling.\n\nSources:\n[1] DOM 14.206 Rev K, Revision Summary; 1.0 PURPOSE; 6.0 PROCEDURE, pp. 1-3: \"6.4.2 Revise a published ETR when the P50 moves by more than 12 h.6.4.3 A move of 12 h or less is logged but not released.\"\n[2] DOM 14.206 Rev K, Revision Summary; 1.0 PURPOSE; 6.0 PROCEDURE, pp. 1-3: \"6.2.3 The ETR Specialist proposes the global ETR on F-DOM-121 with the model inputs attached.6.2.4 The Incident Commander and the Duty Manager approve the global ETR before release. Both signatures go on F-DOM-121.\""
   ],
